{"name":"Toy Submarine Blue","hex":"#005280","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Topoiyo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something to play with, especially as intended for use by a child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A thing of little importance or value; a trifle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toy"},{"term":"submarine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being, relating to, or made for use underwater, especially beneath the sea.","Hidden or undisclosed."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boat that can go underwater.","Alternative form of submarine sandwich."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/submarine"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toy","blocks":[{"text":"A toy or plaything is an object that is used primarily to provide entertainment. Simple examples include toy blocks, board games, and dolls. Toys are often designed for use by children, although many are designed specifically for adults and pets. Toys can provide utilitarian benefits, including physical exercise, cultural awareness, or academic education. Additionally, utilitarian objects, especially those which are no longer needed for their original purpose, can be used as toys. Examples include children building a fort with empty cereal boxes and tissue paper spools, or a toddler playing with a broken TV remote. The term \"toy\" can also be used to refer to utilitarian objects purchased for enjoyment rather than need, or for expensive necessities for which a large fraction of the cost represents its ability to provide enjoyment to the owner, such as luxury cars, high-end motorcycles, gaming computers, and flagship smartphones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Toy_car_%28AM_1996.165.95%29.jpg/330px-Toy_car_%28AM_1996.165.95%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toy","wikidata":"Q11422"},{"title":"Submarine","blocks":[{"text":"A submarine is a watercraft capable of independent operation underwater. The term \"submarine\" is also sometimes used historically or informally to refer to remotely operated vehicles and robots, or to medium-sized or smaller vessels. Submarines are referred to as boats rather than ships regardless of their size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/US_Navy_040730-N-1234E-002_PCU_Virginia_%28SSN_774%29_returns_to_the_General_Dynamics_Electric_Boat_shipyard.jpg/330px-US_Navy_040730-N-1234E-002_PCU_Virginia_%28SSN_774%29_returns_to_the_General_Dynamics_Electric_Boat_shipyard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submarine","wikidata":"Q2811"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg/500px-Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg/1280px-Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg/500px-Little_horse_on_wheels_%28Ancient_greek_child%27s_Toy%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Little horse on wheels, Ancient Greek children's toy. From a tomb dating 950–900 BCE, Kerameikos Archaeological Museum, Athens","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALittle_horse_on_wheels_(Ancient_greek_child's_Toy).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Reif_Spielzeug.jpg/250px-Reif_Spielzeug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/Reif_Spielzeug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Reif_Spielzeug.jpg/250px-Reif_Spielzeug.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A boy with a hoop. Hoops have long been a popular toy across a variety of cultures.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReif_Spielzeug.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/